4️⃣  COMPUTER TROUBLESHOOTING
=====================================

THE MINDSET
  1. Stay calm
  2. Be systematic
  3. Change one thing at a time
  4. Document everything

HARDWARE vs. SOFTWARE PROBLEMS
  Hardware: won't power on, no display, overheating, strange noises
  Software: crashes, error messages, slow system, viruses

THE 6-STEP TROUBLESHOOTING PROCESS
  Step 1 — IDENTIFY    Gather symptoms; note recent changes
  Step 2 — THEORIZE    Start with the simplest explanation
  Step 3 — TEST        One variable at a time; confirm or rule out
  Step 4 — FIX         Back up first; apply carefully
  Step 5 — VERIFY      Confirm fix; check nothing else broke
  Step 6 — DOCUMENT    Record symptom, cause, and solution

COMMON PROBLEMS & QUICK FIXES
  Won't turn on   → Check power cable, outlet, PSU
  No display      → Reseat monitor cable; try another port
  Running slow    → Close apps; restart; scan for malware
  No internet     → Restart router; check Wi-Fi/cables
  Overheating     → Clear dust; check fans
  Blue screen     → Note the error code; undo recent drivers

SAFETY
  DO:    Power down before opening, back up data, work methodically
  DON'T: Work on live power, force connectors, make multiple changes at once

TOOLKIT
  Hardware: screwdrivers, anti-static wrist strap, compressed air
  Software: Task Manager, Device Manager, Antivirus, Safe Mode


=====================================
5️⃣  SOFTWARE TROUBLESHOOTING
=====================================

MINDSET
  Stay calm · Follow a method · Change one thing at a time

THE 6-STEP PROCESS
  Step 1 — DEFINE      What happened? Capture the exact error.
  Step 2 — REPRODUCE   Find reliable steps that trigger it.
  Step 3 — GATHER      Read logs; list recent changes.
  Step 4 — ISOLATE     Test one part at a time; try Safe Mode.
  Step 5 — FIX & TEST  One change; verify; undo if it didn't work.
  Step 6 — DOCUMENT    Record cause, fix, and prevention steps.

COMMON ISSUES & FIXES
  Won't start / crashes  → Restart, update, reinstall; check logs
  Running slow           → Free up disk/memory; close heavy apps
  Frozen                 → End the task; check CPU/memory usage
  Error messages         → Note the exact code; search the precise wording
  Can't connect          → Check network, firewall/VPN; confirm service is up
  Compatibility issues   → Update or roll back; check version requirements

USEFUL TOOLS
  Event Viewer · Task Manager · Ping/network tools · Official docs & forums

BEST PRACTICES
  - Restart first
  - One change at a time
  - Ask "what changed recently?"
  - Back up before big changes
  - Verify the fix fully

WHEN TO ESCALATE
  - Risk of data loss
  - Affects many users
  - Needs permissions you don't have
  - No fix after reasonable effort — hand off with your notes


